# =====================================================================
#  AI API KEYS  (copy this file to ".env" and fill it in)
# =====================================================================
#
#  Step 1: rename/duplicate this file to  .env
#          Windows (PowerShell):  Copy-Item .env.example .env
#          Linux/Mac:             cp .env.example .env
#
#  Step 2: paste your keys below (no quotes, no spaces).
#
#  Step 3: NEVER commit the .env file to Git. The .gitignore ignores it.
#
#  Note: you only need to fill in the keys for the providers you want to
#  test. Providers without a key are skipped automatically.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#  OpenAI  (GPT models)  -  model used: gpt-4.1-mini
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#  How to get it:
#   1. Go to https://platform.openai.com/
#   2. Sign in / create an account.
#   3. Add credit under "Settings > Billing" (calls are paid).
#   4. Open "API keys" (https://platform.openai.com/api-keys).
#   5. Click "Create new secret key", name it and copy the value.
#      The key starts with "sk-...". It is shown only once - copy it now.
OPENAI_API_KEY=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Google Gemini  -  NO SEPARATE KEY NEEDED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Gemini (google/gemini-3.8-flash) runs through OpenRouter in this
#  project, not through the direct Google API. So you do NOT need a
#  Google / AI Studio key - just the OPENROUTER_API_KEY below covers it.
#  (This was done because Google AI Studio billing could not be set up.)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#  OpenRouter  (serves BOTH Gemini and DeepSeek)
#    - google/gemini-3.8-flash
#    - deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3-0324
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#  OpenRouter is an OpenAI-compatible gateway. One key here powers both
#  Gemini and DeepSeek. Both are paid but cheap; the full 20x20x3 run
#  costs roughly US$ 1-2 total, so add a small OpenRouter credit.
#
#  How to get it:
#   1. Go to https://openrouter.ai/
#   2. Sign in (Google/GitHub).
#   3. Add a small credit under "Credits" (a few dollars is plenty).
#   4. Open "Keys" (https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys).
#   5. Click "Create Key", name it and copy the value (starts with
#      "sk-or-..."). Copy it now, it is shown only once.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
